# Forge's route search orders the quests of this guide and its guide writer writes the steps.
# Fixes go into data/route-fixes.json, data/guide-fixes.json or forever-db/corrections, never
# into this file.
# Added here: A Free Lunch (129), Blackrock Blockade (98387).

# Visit 4 of the simulator's consensus Alliance route (Human export,
# 20.5 to 22.7): Stormwind, the road east through Elwynn, Redridge, then
# south to Darkshire. Since 2026-11-07 it comes after Ashenvale, Stonetalon
# and the Wetlands (06-ashenvale, 20-24): the tram from Ironforge brings you
# to Stormwind at about 24.
#
# Flow: Stormwind (training) -> Elwynn road (Theocritus) -> Three Corners -> Lakeridge
# Highway (flight path) -> Lakeshire (hearth, every quest giver) -> the
# sunken chest -> the gnoll hills toward Three Corners -> Deputy
# Feldon -> Lakeshire -> the lake murlocs, Alther's Mill,
# the Blackrock camps east of Stonewatch Keep (a top-up to 23) -> north through
# Galardell Valley, the Old Lion Statue and the watch tower -> Lakeshire ->
# Bellygrub -> Render's Valley and Keeshan -> Lakeshire -> Duskwood.
#
# The Battleworn Axes (20) come from the Blackrock camps at the south end of
# Galardell Valley, east of Stonewatch Keep (about 66-74, 63-86): some 40
# Renegade, Grunt and Outrunner spawns, against about ten east of Alther's
# Mill, which Tazul found too few and too slow to respawn (#340). The keep's
# Sentries and Shadowcasters are elite: the camps lie east of them.
#
# Deviations from the export:
# - Galardell Valley comes after a top-up to level 23 at the Blackrock camps
#   (Duskwood's quests start at 24; Redridge's alone ended at about 21.6,
#   a player's Discord report): its Shadowhide gnolls (median 24) are then
#   within two levels, so Solomon's Law (91), A Watchful Eye (94) and Looking
#   Further (248) are taken on the way back west, and Bellygrub (34, 24) after
#   Lakeshire. Lieutenant Fangore (180, 26) waits for the second pass, at the
#   end of 05-duskwood (#977).
# - Alther's Mill (98386, Forever) is taken from Foreman Oslow when The
#   Everstill Bridge (89) is handed in, at the second Lakeshire stop: he
#   offers it only then (two players' reports; the quest data has no
#   prerequisite for it, #51). The tarantulas are still killed on the trip
#   east.
# - The Lakeshire flight path and hearth (listed at the end of Darkshore in
#   the export) are taken on arrival. The Darkshire flight path and hearth
#   the export lists at the end of this visit belong to the Duskwood guide.
# - Left out, accepted but never turned in on the route: The Price of Shoes
#   (118, Smith Argus in Goldshire) and Theocritus' Retrieval (178, a pendant
#   drop for the Tower of Azora).
# - Refresh (2026): Expanding Horizons (97914, from 03-darkshore) is handed
#   to Baros Alexston at the Stormwind stop; his reply, Making Do (97926),
#   goes back to Auberdine in 30-40/01-hillsbrad-foothills. Baros offers Making Do only
#   after Expanding Horizons (#453), which a player who skipped it in
#   Darkshore does not have, and the project data lists no prerequisite:
#   the accept is optional, so nobody is held at Baros.
# - Lakeshire on arrival: Oslow, Marris, Conacher, the docks (Baren, Wiley),
#   then Breanna and Martie at the west end, one sweep instead of crossing
#   town twice.
#
# Class quests at the Stormwind stop (about level 24): Rogues take Mathias and
# the Defias (2360, Poisons; finished at the end of 05-duskwood), Warlocks
# Devourer of Souls (1716, the Succubus; carried to Takar the Seer in
# 07-thousand-needles), Priests their level 20 spell: Arcane Feedback (5676,
# Human, here), Chastise (5645, Dwarf) and Contingency Plan (94819,
# Gnome) for Ironforge in 06-wetlands, Elune's Grace (5673, Night Elf) for
# Darnassus at the start of 06-wetlands. Night Elf Druids fetch
# the Westfall half pendant for Trial of the Sea Lion (272). Train in
# Stormwind on the way; Shamans take the Deeprun Tram to Ironforge for theirs.
# Paladins: Human Paladins use the Symbol of Life on Henze Faulk by Stone
# Cairn Lake on the road east through Elwynn (The Tome of Divinity, 1786 and
# 1787, from the Stormwind stop of 02-westfall; Redemption at the Stormwind
# stop of 05-duskwood). At 20 Duthorian Rall (Human) or Tiza Battleforge
# (Dwarf) starts The Tome of Valor (1793/1794), the way to Verigan's Fist:
# three dungeons and an escort, the Class guide
# forever/class/paladin/verigans-fist.
#
# Not here: Tharil'zun, Shadow Magic, Wanted: Gath'Ilzogg, WANTED:
# Incinerator Gar'im and Lieutenant Fangore (19, 115, 169, 95999, 180: elite
# or 26) come on the second Redridge pass at the end of 05-duskwood, at about
# 25-26. Not taken: Morganth (249), the Speaking of Fortitude and
# Theocritus' Retrieval chains (343+, 178). Underbelly Scales and Howling in
# the Hills (122, 126) need The Price of Shoes (118, Goldshire turn-in) and A
# Baying of Gnolls (124) first: skipped. The Defias Brotherhood (65), from
# Westfall, is turned in to Wiley the Black in Lakeshire; its follow-up (132)
# leads back to Westfall: not taken.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Stormwind and the road

step Stormwind
  zone Stormwind City
  tip The tram from Ironforge comes in at the Dwarven District. Train and see Baros Alexston, then leave by the main gate and follow the road east through Elwynn Forest.
  train class only Warrior,Paladin,Hunter,Rogue,Priest,Mage,Warlock,Druid -- Level 18 and 20 spells
  turnin 97914                                -- Baros Alexston: Thundris' letter from Auberdine
  accept 97926 optional                       -- Only once Expanding Horizons is handed in: for Thundris Windweaver, back in Auberdine (30-40/01-hillsbrad-foothills)
  vendor nearest

step Woo Ping
  only Warrior
  zone Stormwind City
  when level>=20
  when money>=1g
  when !skill "Polearms" 1
  tip While you're here: learn Polearms from Woo Ping (Trade District, 1 gold); two-handers level a Warrior fastest.
  train 11867                         -- Woo Ping

step Woo Ping
  only Hunter
  zone Stormwind City
  when level>=20
  when money>=1g
  when !skill "Polearms" 1
  tip While you're here: learn Polearms from Woo Ping (Trade District, 1 gold); a Hunter's melee weapon is mostly its stats, and two-handers carry the most.
  train 11867                         -- Woo Ping

step Stormwind class quests
  only Priest,Rogue,Warlock
  zone Stormwind City
  tip Master Mathias Shaw is at SI:7 in Old Town, Gakin the Darkbinder in the Slaughtered Lamb's cellar in the Mage Quarter, High Priestess Laurena in the Cathedral of Light.
  level 20 only Rogue
  accept 2360 only Rogue                      -- Master Mathias Shaw: Agent Kearnen in Westfall takes it, at the end of Duskwood
  level 20 only Warlock
  accept 1716 only Warlock                    -- Gakin the Darkbinder: Takar the Seer in the Barrens takes it, later
  accept 5676 only Human,Priest               -- High Priestess Laurena
  turnin 5676 only Human,Priest               -- Arcane Feedback
  accept 5645 only Dwarf,Priest               -- High Priestess Laurena: High Priest Rohan in Ironforge takes it, later
  accept 94819 npc 376 only Gnome,Priest      -- High Priestess Laurena: High Priestess Mims in Ironforge takes it, later
  accept 5673 only NightElf,Priest            -- High Priestess Laurena: Priestess Alathea in Darnassus takes it, later

step Tram to Ironforge
  only Shaman
  zone Stormwind City
  goto 64.5,7.5 "Tram to Ironforge"

step Shaman training
  only Shaman
  zone Ironforge
  tip Stormwind has no shaman trainer: take the Deeprun Tram from the Dwarven District to Ironforge, train with Eldrun Stormbreaker, then ride the tram back.
  train class

step Fly to Sentinel Hill
  only NightElf,Druid
  zone Stormwind City
  goto 66.3,62.7 "Stormwind flight master"
  fly "Sentinel Hill"

step Half Pendant of Aquatic Endurance
  only NightElf,Druid
  zone Westfall
  tip Fly to Sentinel Hill and head north-west to the coast: the Strange Lockbox lies on the sea floor off the shore. Then head east along the road through Elwynn to Redridge.
  collect 15882 x1                            -- Half Pendant of Aquatic Endurance: the Strange Lockbox

step Back to Elwynn Forest
  only Shaman
  zone Elwynn Forest
  goto 65.2,69.7 "Elwynn Forest"

step Elwynn Forest
  zone Elwynn Forest
  goto 65.2,69.7 "Elwynn Forest"

step Theocritus
  accept 94                           -- On the top floor

step Guard Thomas
  when onquest 35
  turnin 35 only NightElf

step Henze Faulk
  only Human,Paladin
  zone Elwynn Forest
  tip On the road east, past the Tower of Azora, head north from the bridge to Stone Cairn Lake. Henze Faulk lies south of the lake: use the Symbol of Life on him. The Defias Rogue Wizards around him carry the Defias Script.
  use 6866 quest 1786.1 @72.6,51.41 map 1429 era only Human -- Use the Symbol of Life on Henze Faulk
  turnin 1786 only Human -- Henze Faulk
  accept 1787 only Human
  collect 6846 quest 1787.1 only Human -- Defias Script: Defias Rogue Wizards

step Redridge Mountains
  zone Redridge Mountains
